      "side": 1,
      "message": "This will only works if Bluetooth is turned off when having an active device.\n\nI find it suspicious that we:\n* only do that for the last active device\n* only do that for phone / bluetooth reboot and not for each device reconnection\n\nMy other comment on the change where having that into my mind, please let me know what is the reasoning / motivation behind the current implementation. (open discussion !)\n\nI would prefer to have the same pattern, for each reconnection however the disconnection ended (phone reboot / bt reboot, with or without active device, or reconnection to device)\n\nI see that the spec wording is:\n```\nAn equipment safeguard shall prevent exposure of an ordinary person to RS2 power\nsource without intentional physical action from the ordinary person and shall automatically return to an output level not exceeding RS1 when the power is switched off.\n```\nCan we argue that \"the power is switched off\" can applied to the remote device and thus, we need to do it for device reconnection?",
