      "writtenOn": "2025-03-26T17:47:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What about never writing the too high volume on disk ?\n\nSomething like\n```\nvoid storeVolumeForDevice(@NonNull BluetoothDevice device, int storeVolume) {\n        if (mAdapterService.getBondState(device) !\u003d BluetoothDevice.BOND_BONDED) {\n            return;\n        }\n        mVolumeMap.put(device, storeVolume);          ////// Do we want the volume to be high for quick reconnection ?\n        \n        if (storeVolume \u003e safeVolume) {\n            Log.w(TAG, \"Override persistent saving for unsafe volume for device \" + device);\n            storeVolume \u003d safeVolume;\n        }\n        SharedPreferences.Editor pref \u003d getVolumeMap().edit();\n        mVolumeEventLogger.logd(\n                TAG,\n                \"storeVolume: Storing stream volume level for device \"\n                        + device\n                        + \" : \"\n                        + storeVolume);\n        pref.putInt(device.getAddress(), storeVolume);\n        // Always use apply() since it is asynchronous, otherwise the call can hang waiting for\n        // storage to be written.\n        pref.apply();\n}\n```",
